    "subtasks": [],
    "description": "*Scenario:*\r\n\r\nWhile configuring a Cart Range Percent Discount for promotions, there doesn’t seem to be an out-of-the-box option to set a maximum discount cap. For instance, if the business wants to offer a 15% discount on the cart total, but with a maximum discount limit of $100 irrespective of the cart value, the system currently applies the percentage across the total cart value without a ceiling.\r\n\r\nThe primary aim is not to enforce a minimum margin rule for the product price but to set a maximum discount limit regardless of the cart total particularly for the high valued cart totals. \r\n\r\nThe requirement also considers a case whereby system is applying single cart promotion at a time just to simplify the scenario.\r\n\r\n*Solution Proposal:*\r\nExtending the ProductPromoAction entity with maxDiscountAmount field and considering this configuration in the promotion engine to validate the max discount that can be provided to the customer.",
